{title: O Praise the Name (Anástasis) (FJ_48_en)}
{song_number: 48}
{language: en}

{start_of_verse: 1}
I cast my [G]mind to Calvary where Jesus
[D]bled and died for [Em]me. I see His
[C]wounds, His hands, His feet, my Saviour
[D]on that cursed [G]tree.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
His body [G]bound and drenched in tears, they laid Him
[D]down in Joseph's [Em]tomb. The entrance [C]sealed
by heavy stone, Messiah [D]still and all a[G]lone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [G]praise the Name of the [C]Lord our [G]God.
O [Em]praise His Name for[Dsus4]ever[D]more.
For [G/B]endless days we will [C]sing Your [Em]praise:
Oh [C]Lord, oh [D]Lord our [G]God.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Then on the [G]third at break of dawn, [D]the Son of Heaven
rose a[Em]gain. O [C]trampled death, where is your sting?
The [D]angels roar for Christ the [G]King.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [G]praise the Name of the [C]Lord our [G]God.
O [Em]praise His Name for[Dsus4]ever[D]more.
For [G/B]endless days we will [C]sing Your [Em]praise:
Oh [C]Lord, oh [D]Lord our [G]God.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 4}
He shall re[G]turn in robes of white, the [D]blazing sun
shall pierce the [Em]night. And I will [C]rise among the saints,
my [D]gaze transfixed on Jesus' [G]face.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [G]praise the Name of the [C]Lord our [G]God.
O [Em]praise His Name for[Dsus4]ever[D]more.
For [G/B]endless days we will [C]sing Your [Em]praise:
Oh [C]Lord, oh [D]Lord our [G]God.
{end_of_chorus}
